HST Office: in the Styles gallery, the arrow keys go on past the visible previews and Enter applies.

The gallery shows one page of previews (one at 1366-1485 px). The arrow keys stopped at the edge of the
page, so with one preview Right did nothing, and Enter (the icon view's "activate", shared with a double
click) opened the Modify Style dialog instead of applying the style. Now:
- Right on the last preview of a page goes on to the next style and Left on the first back to the previous
  one, paging as needed, and the style is applied as an arrow key inside a page does;
- Enter and a double click apply the focused style, as in Office; Modify Style stays in the context menu.

- svx StylesPreviewWindow: ApplyStyle (shared by click, arrows and Enter), HstKeyPressHdl.

